    {
      "id": "exam/edexcel-9fm0-02-2021-november/q4",
      "question": "<p>In this question you may assume the results for</p><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\sum_{r=1}^{n}r^3,\\quad\\sum_{r=1}^{n}r^2\\quad\\text{and}\\quad\\sum_{r=1}^{n}r\" data-display=\"true\"></div><ol class=\"parts\"><li>Show that the sum of the cubes of the first <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n\"></span> positive odd numbers is<div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"n^2(2n^2-1)\" data-display=\"true\"></div><span class=\"marks\">(5)</span></li></ol><p>The sum of the cubes of 10 consecutive positive odd numbers is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"99\\,800\"></span></p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"2\"><li>Use the answer to part (a) to determine the smallest of these 10 consecutive positive odd numbers. <span class=\"marks\">(4)</span></li></ol>",
