    {
      "id": "exam/edexcel-9fm0-02-2021-november/q6",
      "question": "<p>The curve <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C\"></span> has equation</p><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"r=a(p+2\\cos\\theta)\\qquad 0\\leqslant\\theta&lt;2\\pi\" data-display=\"true\"></div><p>where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"p\"></span> are positive constants and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"p&gt;2\"></span></p><p>There are exactly four points on <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C\"></span> where the tangent is perpendicular to the initial line.</p><ol class=\"parts\"><li>Show that the range of possible values for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"p\"></span> is<div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"2&lt;p&lt;4\" data-display=\"true\"></div><span class=\"marks\">(5)</span></li><li>Sketch the curve with equation<div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"r=a(3+2\\cos\\theta)\\qquad 0\\leqslant\\theta&lt;2\\pi\\qquad\\text{where }a&gt;0\" data-display=\"true\"></div><span class=\"marks\">(1)</span></li></ol><p>John digs a hole in his garden in order to make a pond.</p><p>The pond has a uniform horizontal cross section that is modelled by the curve with equation</p><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"r=20(3+2\\cos\\theta)\\qquad 0\\leqslant\\theta&lt;2\\pi\" data-display=\"true\"></div><p>where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"r\"></span> is measured in centimetres.</p><p>The depth of the pond is 90 centimetres.</p><p>Water flows through a hosepipe into the pond at a rate of 50 litres per minute.</p><p>Given that the pond is initially empty,</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"3\"><li>determine how long it will take to completely fill the pond with water using the hosepipe, according to the model. Give your answer to the nearest minute. <span class=\"marks\">(7)</span></li><li>State a limitation of the model. <span class=\"marks\">(1)</span></li></ol>",
      "steps": [
