    {
      "id": "exam/edexcel-9fm0-02-2021-november/q7",
      "question": "<p><strong>Solutions based entirely on graphical or numerical methods are not acceptable.</strong></p><figure class=\"practice-figure\" style=\"max-width:75mm;margin:2mm auto\"><img src=\"resources/exams/edexcel-9fm0-02-2021-november/q07-figure.svg\" alt=\"Figure 1: the curve y = arsinh x for x &gt;= 0 from the origin O and the dashed horizontal line y = beta; the region R between the curve, the y-axis and the line y = beta is shaded.\"></figure><p>Figure 1 shows a sketch of part of the curve with equation</p><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"y=\\operatorname{arsinh}x\\qquad x\\geqslant 0\" data-display=\"true\"></div><p>and the straight line with equation <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=\\beta\"></span></p><p>The line and the curve intersect at the point with coordinates <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(\\alpha,\\beta)\"></span></p><p>Given that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\beta=\\dfrac12\\ln 3\"></span></p><ol class=\"parts\"><li>show that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\alpha=\\dfrac{1}{\\sqrt3}\"></span> <span class=\"marks\">(3)</span></li></ol><p>The finite region <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"R\"></span>, shown shaded in Figure 1, is bounded by the curve with equation <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=\\operatorname{arsinh}x\"></span>, the <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y\"></span>-axis and the line with equation <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=\\beta\"></span></p><p>The region <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"R\"></span> is rotated through <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"2\\pi\"></span> radians about the <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y\"></span>-axis.</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"2\"><li>Use calculus to find the exact value of the volume of the solid generated. <span class=\"marks\">(6)</span></li></ol>",
