      "id": "exam/edexcel-9fm0-02-2021-november/q8",
      "question": "<ol class=\"parts\" type=\"i\"><li>The point <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"P\"></span> is one vertex of a regular pentagon in an Argand diagram.<br>The centre of the pentagon is at the origin.<p>Given that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"P\"></span> represents the complex number <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"6+6\\mathrm i\"></span>, determine the complex numbers that represent the other vertices of the pentagon, giving your answers in the form <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"r\\mathrm e^{\\mathrm i\\theta}\"></span> <span class=\"marks\">(5)</span></p></li><li><ol class=\"parts\"><li>On a single Argand diagram, shade the region, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"R\"></span>, that satisfies both<div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\left|z-2\\mathrm i\\right|\\leqslant 2\\qquad\\text{and}\\qquad\\frac14\\pi\\leqslant\\arg z\\leqslant\\frac13\\pi\" data-display=\"true\"></div><span class=\"marks\">(2)</span></li><li>Determine the exact area of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"R\"></span>, giving your answer in simplest form. <span class=\"marks\">(4)</span></li></ol></li></ol>",
